---
// ⚠️ DRAFT FOR LEGAL REVIEW — not final legal text. Have a lawyer / DPO check
// it (GDPR + Greek law 4624/2019 + ePrivacy) before relying on it, and fill in
// the [bracketed] items (GA4 retention, form retention).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import MenuOverlay from "../components/MenuOverlay.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy & cookie policy — Untitled Office" description="How Untitled Office uses cookies, Google Analytics, session recording and contact-form data.">
  <MenuOverlay />
  <Header />
  <main>
    <article class="pv edge">
      <h1 class="pv-title">Privacy &amp; cookie policy</h1>
      <p class="pv-meta mono">Last updated: 25-11-2026</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website is run by Untitled Office, Ippokratous 7, 106 79 Athens, Greece.
        For anything about your data, email <a class="u-link" href="mailto:info@untitledoffice.gr" data-umami-event="contact_click" data-umami-event-type="email">info@untitledoffice.gr</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Analytics (only with your consent).</strong> If you allow analytics cookies, we use
        Google Analytics 4, loaded through Google Tag Manager, to understand how the site is used:
        pages visited, time on page, how you arrived (for example a search or a link), device and
        browser type, and approximate location (country and city). With analytics consent, we also
        count interactions on each page (mouse movements, scrolls, clicks, touches and key presses,
        as counts only, never which keys) to tell human visitors from automated or bot traffic, and
        send these counts to Google Analytics as a “behaviour summary”. Google Analytics 4 does not store
        IP addresses. We don’t use this data for advertising. If you also allow session recording, we
        link it to your recordings (see below); we don’t combine it with any other data. It is kept for
        [14 months — set in our GA4 account].
      </p>
      <p>
        Without your consent, Google Tag Manager still loads, but analytics cookies are not set.
        Google may receive limited, cookieless signals (Consent Mode) that cannot identify you.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cookieless statistics (no consent needed).</strong> For basic visitor numbers we also
        use Umami Cloud, which runs for every visitor. It sets no cookies and stores nothing on your
        device. It collects anonymous, aggregated usage data only (pages viewed, referring site,
        browser, device type and country) and some interactions, such as which project or link was
        clicked, never anything you type or your contact details. It can’t identify you, isn’t used for
        profiling and isn’t combined with other data. We rely on our legitimate interest in
        understanding, at an aggregate level, how the site is used (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Contact form.</strong> When you send the contact form, we receive the details you
        enter (name, telephone, e-mail, website, budget and your message). The form is handled by
        Netlify Forms, our hosting provider, which stores the submission and forwards it to us. We
        use it only to reply to your enquiry and keep it for as long as needed for that
        [and any follow-up work].
      </p>

      <h2>Session recording and AI analysis</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Only with your separate consent.</strong> Session recording is its own choice in the
        cookie settings (“Session recording”), separate from analytics and off unless you turn it on.
        If you do, we record your visit to see how the site is used. A recording captures your clicks, scrolling, the pages you
        view and what appears on your screen while you’re here. It also notes the page that sent you
        here (the referrer) and any campaign tags in the link you followed (UTM tags, such as source,
        medium and campaign).
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What we don’t record.</strong> Anything you type into a field, such as the contact
        form, is masked and never recorded.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Why.</strong> To understand how visitors move through the site, for example whether
        someone who looks at a project then visits the Contact page, so we can improve it. We don’t
        use recordings for advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Who processes it.</strong> The recording library is served from our own website, not
        from a third-party CDN. Recordings are stored with Netlify (Netlify Blobs), our
        hosting provider. We analyse them with Google’s Gemini AI to find patterns such as “viewed a
        project, then visited Contact”, and send those results to our Google Analytics 4 property.
        We may also use Anthropic’s Claude AI to analyse the recorded timeline of a visit; typed text
        is never recorded, so it is never part of that analysis. If you have also allowed analytics, each recording is linked to your Google Analytics client
        ID and session ID, so the results can be matched to your visit there.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>How long we keep it.</strong> Recordings are kept for 12 months, then deleted. We
        keep them this long so we can compare how visitors use the site across seasons and over the
        year. The results sent to Google Analytics are kept as described above.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Legal basis and withdrawing consent.</strong> Session recording is based on your
        consent to the “Session recording” category specifically (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)); allowing
        analytics alone does not turn it on, and without it nothing is recorded. You can withdraw
        consent at any time through “Cookie settings” in the footer: recording stops from then on and
        its session-storage keys are removed. To have a recording deleted sooner, email us.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <div class="pv-table-wrap">
        <table class="pv-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th><th>Type</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>cc_cookie</code></td><td>Remembers your cookie choice</td><td>6 months</td><td>Necessary</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Tells visits apart (Google Analytics)</td><td>2 years</td><td>Analytics, with consent</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code></td><td>Keeps session state (Google Analytics)</td><td>2 years</td><td>Analytics, with consent</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>uo_rec_sid</code></td><td>Recording session ID (session storage, not a cookie)</td><td>Until you close the tab</td><td>Session recording, with consent</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>uo_rec_src</code></td><td>Traffic source of the visit: referrer and UTM tags (session storage, not a cookie)</td><td>Until you close the tab</td><td>Session recording, with consent</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>We also remember your light/dark and colour choice in your browser’s local storage; this is not sent to us.</p>

      <h2>Legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics cookies are used only with your consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) and the ePrivacy rules).
        Session recording and its AI analysis are used only with your separate consent to the
        “Session recording” category (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) and the ePrivacy rules).
        The consent cookie is strictly necessary to remember your choice. Umami’s cookieless,
        anonymous statistics are based on our legitimate interest (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)). Contact-form data is used
        to answer your request (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)).
      </p>

      <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
      <p>
        You can change or withdraw consent at any time:
        <button type="button" class="pv-btn u-link" data-cc-settings>open cookie settings</button>
        (also linked in the footer). If you switch analytics off, we remove the Google Analytics cookies.
        If you switch session recording off, we stop recording your visits and remove its session-storage keys.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else processes data</h2>
      <p>
        Google (Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, Gemini AI), Anthropic (Claude AI, analysis of
        session recordings), Umami Software (Umami Cloud statistics) and Netlify (hosting, forms and
        session-recording storage) process data on our behalf. Some of this may happen outside the EU, under the safeguards these providers
        offer (such as the EU–US Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses).
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us for access to, correction or deletion of your data, or object to or restrict
        its use, by emailing <a class="u-link" href="mailto:info@untitledoffice.gr" data-umami-event="contact_click" data-umami-event-type="email">info@untitledoffice.gr</a>.
        You can also complain to the Hellenic Data Protection Authority (dpa.gr).
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .pv {
    max-width: calc(44rem + 2 * var(--edge));
    padding-top: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }
  .pv-title {
    font-family: var(--ff-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .pv-meta { color: var(--muted); margin: 1rem 0 0; }
  .pv h2 {
    font-family: var(--ff-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.6vw, 1.5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .pv p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 1em; }
  .pv strong { font-weight: 500; }
  .pv-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 1em; }
  .pv-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .pv-table th,
  .pv-table td { text-align: left; padding: 0.55rem 1rem 0.55rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); vertical-align: top; }
  .pv-table th { font-weight: 500; }
  .pv-table code { font-family: var(--ff-mono); font-size: 0.85em; }
  .pv-btn { background: none; border: 0; padding: 0; font: inherit; color: inherit; cursor: pointer; }
</style>
